# Delete session

Plain live tmux sessions are closeable, but not deletable: there is no
associated checkout for `C-d` to remove.

    :b jj tmux cat (available)
    :t rename-session -t 0 runner (success)
    :t new-session -d -s alpha "cat" (success)
    :t new-session -d -s alpine "cat" (success)
    :t new-session -d -s ui "smth; cat" (success)
    :t resize-window -t ui:0 -x 120 -y 10 (success)
    :p ui:0.0
    :settle (settled)

Filter to the matching sessions. The first match, `alpha`, is selected. The
footer should offer `C-x` close, but not `C-d` delete.

    :k alp
    :snap

```terminal
session: alp
  2/4 | [C-r] repo: none
▌■ alpha                                                                                                               ┃
 [C-x] close, [C-f] flag
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────





```

Pressing `C-d` should do nothing for a plain live tmux session.

    :k C-d
    :settle (settled)
    :snap --color

```terminal
session: alp
  2/4 | [C-r] repo: none
▌■ alpha                                                                                                               ┃
 [C-x] close, [C-f] flag
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────





```

![light](delete-session.md.snap.2.light.svg)
![dark](delete-session.md.snap.2.dark.svg)

The session should still exist, and the picker should still be running.

    :t has-session -t alpha (success)
    :t has-session -t ui (success)

